"The prognosis is influenced by several factors. Positive lymph node metastasis and the presence of lymphovascular invasion are concerning findings. The Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3) noted in the prostatectomy specimen contributes to risk stratification. Conversely, negative surgical margins and no seminal vesicle invasion are favorable elements. Preoperative PSA was 3.3 ng/mL, which is a relatively low value. Biopsy-to-prostatectomy differences are not explicitly detailed as the biopsy Gleason pattern and ISUP report are missing. Nodal status was determined with metastasis present. The prognosis remains subject to revision based on postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory over time. The fixed estimated horizon is 69.39 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 55.52–83.27 months; its coverage has not been validated."
